   "text": "Okay, so I filled it with coolant, brought it up to temperature, got it super hot, um, you know, checked the radiator, checked underneath, checked all the hoses, and it actually was not leaking coolant at all. Um, so what I think happened i- is it obviously rolled upside down. Um, there's this vent hose right here, and when it was upside down, the pressure caused a bunch of that coolant to get pushed out of this vent hose, making it just go absolutely everywhere. And so, um, 'cause if you look on the skid plate, it's pretty, it's pretty, uh, moist everywhere. So coolant did get a lot of places, um, but I think it was just that pressure upside down that did it",
